Screened 115 queued papers using title and abstract; 104 proceed to quote-backed judgments.

Tier C exclusions:
2609.38662: Retrains the collaboration director across rounds; the abstract does not establish persistent non-weight collaboration artifacts beyond its learned policy.
2610.08621: Iteratively refines generated games; no persistent change to the agent harness across game-development tasks is established.
2610.13058: Trains execution and reflection policies while reusing abandoned-branch knowledge within ongoing tasks; cross-task harness persistence is not established.
2610.13098: Retains program-render records within individual graphics tasks and repairs outputs without establishing later-task harness changes.
2610.14523: Audits a fixed medical segmentation component; recursive harness optimization is specified but unexecuted and no self-improvement mechanism is evaluated.
2610.14625: Surveys self-improvement design dimensions and proposes research directions without implementing a persistent update loop.
2610.18842: Surveys physical self-improvement and proposes evidence levels; no implemented persistent harness improvement method.
2610.20344: Benchmarks one-shot harness construction against scripted behavioral tests, without a self-modification or persistent feedback-driven improvement loop.
2610.22192: Verified trajectory rewriting and critic-inheriting reinforcement learning consolidate improvements into policy weights; no retained non-weight self-modification is described.
2610.22289: Compares developer-supplied fixed prompt and controller variants; agents do not modify and retain their own harness components.
2610.23194: Organizational simulation generates persistent work context and training data, but reported learning updates model weights without a self-modifying harness loop.

No suspected instruction injection detected.
